comment.narrative:
•479 complaints were processed across the KNCHR regions;
•293 of those complaints were by male complainants while 175 were by females and 3 related to intersex persons;
•Ten complaints (5%) of the total complaints received were by or relating to rights of PWDs;
•Five (5) Joint public complaints handling initiatives held in Machakos, Mathare, Kisumu, Bungoma and Mombasa;
•At least 170 members of the public sensitized on human rights complaints processing;
•134 complaints received and processed towards resolution.

•One (1) consultative workshop with Teachers Service Commission (TSC) representatives on the rights of intersex children and adults in Kenya;
•Advocacy and Public awareness forums in Nakuru, Kisii; Taita Taveta; Wajir; and Marsabit Counties;
•Finalization of Global Citizenship Education Research Report-Focus on Rights of Intersex Children.
